From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ricktav <82380971+ricktav@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 08:05:50 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: apple: s5l8960x: Describe the D2089 charger input
 and charge timer

The A7 iPads' Lightning charger now keeps the D2089's input-suspend bit
(0x10 bit 2) in step with the input limit and restarts the charge timer
at 0x4c8, as iOS 12 does. Give it register 0x10 as its "input" range and
extend the control range from 0x4c0 to 0x4c8, in the iPad Air's and the
iPad mini 2's shared files.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: ricktav <82380971+ricktav@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/s5l8960x-air1.dtsi  | 9 +++++++--
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/s5l8960x-mini2.dtsi | 9 +++++++--
 2 files changed, 14 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/s5l8960x-air1.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/s5l8960x-air1.dtsi
index a886fbafe..a530dedd3 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/s5l8960x-air1.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/s5l8960x-air1.dtsi
@@ -161,8 +161,13 @@ pmu_events: interrupt-controller {
 	 */
 	tristar_charger: charger@60 {
 		compatible = "apple,d2089-tristar-charger";
-		reg = <0x60 0x0d>, <0x4c0 0x01>, <0x500 0x04>;
-		reg-names = "status", "control", "adc";
+		/*
+		 * The control bank reaches the charge timer at 0x4c8; bit 2 of
+		 * 0x10 suspends the charger input, as iOS 12 sets it with every
+		 * input-limit write.
+		 */
+		reg = <0x60 0x0d>, <0x4c0 0x09>, <0x500 0x04>, <0x10 0x01>;
+		reg-names = "status", "control", "adc", "input";
 		interrupt-parent = <&pmu_events>;
 		/*
 		 * The PMU line and ADC done. No source events, as on the iPad
diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/s5l8960x-mini2.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/s5l8960x-mini2.dtsi
index de928e2ba..831a8cc69 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/s5l8960x-mini2.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/s5l8960x-mini2.dtsi
@@ -117,8 +117,13 @@ pmu_events: interrupt-controller {
 	 */
 	tristar_charger: charger@60 {
 		compatible = "apple,d2089-tristar-charger";
-		reg = <0x60 0x0d>, <0x4c0 0x01>, <0x500 0x04>;
-		reg-names = "status", "control", "adc";
+		/*
+		 * The control bank reaches the charge timer at 0x4c8; bit 2 of
+		 * 0x10 suspends the charger input, as iOS 12 sets it with every
+		 * input-limit write.
+		 */
+		reg = <0x60 0x0d>, <0x4c0 0x09>, <0x500 0x04>, <0x10 0x01>;
+		reg-names = "status", "control", "adc", "input";
 		interrupt-parent = <&pmu_events>;
 		/*
 		 * The PMU line and ADC done. No source events, as on the iPad
